# Strings slopcheck must skip, one exact substring per line.
#
# Run:  python3 ~/.claude/skills/stop-slop/scripts/slopcheck.py \
#           --allow-file .slopcheck-allow src/services/agents/AgentHelpContent.qml
#
# ROADMAP.md §41 (line 1601): "Do not stop-slop machine interfaces. Preserve
# literal commands, code identifiers, paths, config keys, API names, protocol
# fields, logs and technical values when changing them would reduce
# correctness." Each entry below is one of those, or a QML keyword.
#
# Rule: an entry names the identifier, never a sentence of prose. Allowing a
# whole sentence would exempt every future edit to that sentence too.

# QML's own keyword. `readonly property` is how a singleton declares an
# immutable property; slopcheck reads the -ly and calls it an adverb.
readonly property

# The product name for the Config toggle in ROADMAP.md §42.1, which the help
# has to call by its name or the user cannot find the setting.
Always Unrestricted

# The break-glass flag from ROADMAP.md §3.4 and §4.5. "everything" is in the
# flag, not in the prose describing it.
--unsafe-everything
